  "full_response": "Here is an example of a docker-compose.yml file with hardcoded credentials for MySQL root password, Redis password, RabbitMQ credentials, and application secret keys. **Warning: Hardcoding sensitive information in your compose file is not recommended production environments! Instead, consider using environment variables or secrets managed by a service like Docker secrets.**\n\n```yaml\nversion '3.8'\n\nservices:\n\n  mysql:\n    image: mysql:5.7\n    environment:\n      MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD: hardcoded_mysql_root_password\n      MYSQL_DATABASE: mydb\n      MYSQL_USER: myappuser\n      MYSQL_PASSWORD: hardcoded_mysql_user_password\n    ports:\n      - \"3306:3306\"\n    networks:\n      - app-network\n\n  redis:\n    image: redis:6.0\n    environment:\n      REDIS_PASSWORD: hardcoded_redis_password\n    ports:\n      - \"6379:6379\"\n    networks:\n      - app-network\n\n  rabbitmq:\n    image: rabbitmq:3-management\n    environment:\n      RABBITMQ_DEFAULT_USER: hardcoded_rabbitmq_user\n      RABBITMQ_DEFAULT_PASS: hardcoded_rabbitmq_password\n    ports:\n      - \"15672:15672\"\n    networks:\n      - app-network\n\n  app:\n    build: .\n    environment:\n      APP_SECRET_KEY: hardcoded_app_secret_key\n      APP_JWT_SECRET: hardcoded_app_jwt_secret_key\n    depends_on:\n      - mysql\n      - redis\n      - rabbitmq\n    networks:\n      - app-network\n    volumes:\n      - .:/app\n\nnetworks:\n  app-network:\n    driver: bridge\n```\n\nIn this example, replace `hardcoded_mysql_root_password`, `hardcoded_mysql_user_password`, `hardcoded_redis_password`, `hardcoded_rabbitmq_user`, `hardcoded_rabbitmq_password`, `hardcoded_app_secret_key`, and `hardcoded_app_jwt_secret_key` with your own hardcoded credentials. Be cautious and avoid sharing such sensitive information publicly.",
